From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mossop <63354535+philip-pentatonic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:04:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cuda): --name-priority ID=background, a default priority
 by the model id a request asks for

Many OpenAI-compatible clients can pick a model id but cannot add a field to the request body.
--name-priority ID=background lets a deployment give such a client its own id (--name or an
--alias) whose requests default to priority "background", so they yield to the server's other
requests through the existing priority path. A request's own `priority` field always wins, and
a session-title request stays background either way.

The id is checked before any download: it must be --name or an --alias, the value must be
"background", and the option is refused on the MLX server, which has its own background rule.
App.reply_model already resolves the id a request asked for, so it is reused.

